Hi everyone!  I've been playing nethack on and off for a few years
now, but only recently have I begun making extensive use of the
spoilers and begun to make real progress in the game (previously, the
furthest that I had gotten was completing the Valkyrie quest and
killing medusa, then dying stupidly after that).

I've become attached to my current character and I'm looking for some
advice as to what to do before attacking the castle.  Currently, my
Valkyrie looks like:
Level 17, 165HP, AC:-23, crowned
wielding Excalibur
+0 GDSM, +0 cloak of protection, oilskin cloak but not worn right now,
no other special armor aside from bonuses
rings of free action & levitation
blessed greased BoH
identified scrolls of charging and 2 magic markers, 0:7 & 0:47
crowned

Question #1: I'm having serious issues with item identification. Up
until the last ~2000 turns I had only found 2 scrolls of
identification, and after blessing each only identified a few items. I
burned 35 charges of a MM writing identify scrolls and blessing them,
and none of them identified all. Is it worthwhile to burn more charges
on a MM, and possibly use an already identified scroll of charging to
charge it back up, in an attempt to identify all of my loot? I mostly
want to identify scrolls of genocide so that I can get rid of liches
in the castle... I'm afraid of them (I fell down to the castle at some
point and a master lich teleported over to me -- nothing bad happened
b/c I happened to fall down right next to the up-stairs, but any
monster that can teleport to greet you seems like it should be taken
seriously).  While I've managed to identify some things, I've got a
bunch of rings that would be nice to identify, some wands, and a whole
bunch of scrolls and potions still (I haven't id'd enchant weapon &
armor yet -- sitting on a throne yielded a wish and the GDSM).

Question #2: Will a wand of cancellation take care of liches' magical
attacks? I've got a 0:7 wand of cancellation, and maybe this is better
than worrying about genocide as above.

Question #3: I only recently discovered the joys of #twoweapon. Right
now, I'm wielding Excalibur and a +0 silver saber, but I don't know if
it would be better to wield a +1 dagger instead of the silver saber
(I'm expert in dagger, and maxed out at basic in saber).  Or, if I
make it through the castle I could wish for a shield and just wield
Excalibur. So the question is, should I continue with #twoweapon, or
switch to a weapon & shield?  If I do #twoweapon, should I use the
saber or a dagger as my backup?  Am I right to assume that the silver
saber will be better down below the castle, even though I can only
advance it to basic and not expert as with the dagger?

Question #4: What should my wishing priorities be if I make it through
the castle?  My plan is:
1. reflection -- either amulet or shield, depending on answers to
above
2. amulet of life saving, if I go with the shield (figure it's a good
idea for someone that's never gotten a character this far)
3. speed boots
4. gauntlets of power
???

Useful things that I can think of -- a cloak of displacement, a weapon
